  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice.\r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: \r\rE01\rE02\rE03\rP01 Rev 2 \rP02 Rev 2 \rP03 Rev 2 \rP04 Rev 2\rP05 Rev 2 \rLocation Plan\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The external finishing materials shall match those used in the construction of the existing building and/or areas of hard surfacing. \r\rReason: To ensure a satisfactory appearance\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted, unless otherwise submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, cycle parking must be provided in compliance with the following criteria: \r\r- Provision of four long stay cycle parking spaces \r- in an accessible location: the access route to the store should be a minimum of 1.2m wide to enable the bike to enter the store, should be step free and involve no more than 2 doors or gate (excluding the store door).\r- Secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob\r- Fully enclosed\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.",
    "Notwithstanding the submitted sustainability statement, prior to commencement of above ground works. a detailed energy statement confirming the CO2/yr (using SAP 10) reduction over Part L of Building Regulations (2021) shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The Energy Statement shall follow the GLA's Energy Assessment Guidance, the 'be lean, be clean, be green' reduction hierarchy set out in the London Plan (2021), and aspire to achieve a 35% reduction over Part L of Building Regulations (2021). \r\rThe renewable energy technologies included in the Energy Statement shall be incorporated into the development and installed in accordance with the recommendations of Energy Statement prior to first occupation of the development.\r\rReason: In the interest of sustainable development and to ensure that the Local Planning Authority may be satisfied that CO2 emission reduction targets are met in accordance with Policy DMD51 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014).\r\r\r\r\r\r"
  ],
